Subject: [PATCH] HWUI: use stock hardware bitmap snapshots on the host

The host now provides AImageReader, native buffer queues and RenderProxy.
Enable the original implementation through those native interfaces instead
of overriding HardwareRenderer JNI with a Kotlin HardwareBufferRenderer.
The host Skia import must run on the owning render thread. Bind Bitmap's
color-space factory to the existing native RenderProxy import at that seam,
leaving the snapshot's AImageReader / RenderProxy algorithm intact.

--- a/libs/hwui/jni/android_graphics_HardwareRenderer.cpp
+++ b/libs/hwui/jni/android_graphics_HardwareRenderer.cpp
@@ -731,6 +731,6 @@
 static jobject android_view_ThreadedRenderer_createHardwareBitmapFromRenderNode(JNIEnv* env,
         jobject clazz, jlong renderNodePtr, jint jwidth, jint jheight) {
-#ifdef __ANDROID__
+#if defined(__ANDROID__) || defined(ARTZIG_HOST_GRAPHICS)
     RenderNode* renderNode = reinterpret_cast<RenderNode*>(renderNodePtr);
     if (jwidth <= 0 || jheight <= 0) {
         ALOGW("Invalid width %d or height %d", jwidth, jheight);

